eld manual-drain promise — real claimed pre-edit item across the edit, stale_discarded directly asserted (anti-shim satisfied); --message/--message-id aliases; tool_call edit content-verbatim noted for Story 6.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:3:Companion to `tech-design.md`. Maps all 46 TCs to test files with setup and assertion. Conventions carried from Epic 01: real SQLite (temp dirs, no mocks of internal modules), TC ids in test titles, the deterministic provider double injected at the same seam production uses, process-spawned CLI tests under `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:7:**Provider double** (`test/fixtures/provider-double.ts`): implements all seven `DerivationProvider` operations as marked input-derived output — `smoothed(…)`, `toolcall(…)`, `toolresult(…)`, `rendering(…)`, `projection(…)`, `detailed(…)`, `brief(…)` wrapping a deterministic digest of the input. Scripting API per test: `failNext(n, { retryable })`, `failKind(kind, n)`, `delayKind(kind, ms)`, `captureInputs()`. Determinism of the double itself is asserted in `fixtures.test.ts` (same input → same output, twice).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:9:**Thread builders** (`test/fixtures/threads.ts`, extended): `threadWithClosedTurns(n, opts)`, `threadWithToolRun(opts)` (call+result pairs, error variants, missing-result variant), `threadWithChunks(policyOverride)` — all built through real intake, then drained with the double as needed. Multi-state fixture: builds a thread, scripts the double to fail selected kinds past budget, drains, yielding every form state in one file.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:11:**SDK construction in tests:** `createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \"manual\", retry: { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 0, backoffCapMs: 0 }, lease: { durationMs: 200 } })` unless a test says otherwise. Background-mode tests construct with `mode: \"background\"` and await `drainSettled`. Spawned CLI process tests set `LHC_PROVIDER` to the deterministic provider registered through the same named-provider registry production uses; no spawned test injects a provider through a test-only path.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:44:| TC-2.1 | Intake prompt; drain | `smoothed_prompt` ready; content === double's deterministic output for the prompt text |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:45:| TC-2.2 | Intake `tool_call` event | Batch result lists `tool_call_summary` item; intake return precedes any handler run (double's capture log empty at return); after drain: summary ready, contains tool name + args digest |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:47:| TC-2.4 | Three variants: result ok / result isError / call without result; identical double text for all three | Outcomes `succeeded` / `failed` / `unknown` respectively, read from `derived_form.metadata` — not parsed from `content` — proving outcome is record-derived, text-independent, and machine-readable apart from provider prose |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:74:| TC-4.4 | Failed smoothing; `messages.requeue`; drain healthy | Form ready; reason cleared; source version incremented; requeue inserted the deterministic id for the current source version without collision (the failed item's row was deleted at exhaustion — DD-1) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:75:| TC-4.5 | Requeue same form twice before drain | First `{workItemId}`, second `{noop: \"already_queued\"}`; one live item in queue read |\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:63:// proof of durability (anti-shim requirement).\npackages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts:118:    // Durable read-back through the owning domain: deterministic ids, status\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:24:**Key constraint:** Inference is slow, non-deterministic, and can fail; the conversation never waits on it. Derived gaps degrade reads; they never block them. Only damage to the source record stops anything.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:52:- The provider seam: a semantic inference interface injected at SDK construction, with a deterministic test double; provider calls never inside transactions\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:64:- Real provider adapters (model choice, prompt text, API clients are adapter concerns; this epic ships the seam and the double)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:75:| A4 | Smoothing and summary quality is an adapter/prompt concern; this epic's tests assert presence, state, and mechanical properties of derived forms, not prose quality | Validated | Lee | Provider double returns deterministic marked output |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:106:- **TC-1.2** (AC-1.2): Start a drain on a slow item (double with latency), queue two more mid-flight → all three processed; scheduling shows one coalesced follow-up pass.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:112:- **TC-1.8** (AC-1.9): Double fails an item twice then succeeds → artifact ready; double fails past the budget → artifact failed with final reason, next item ran.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:129:- **AC-2.2**: A tool-call message's summary work lands a summary naming the tool and describing its arguments, with an outcome field; a `tool_call` event in an intake batch queues a `tool_call_summary` work item the same way Epic 01 queues the other message-level kinds — an additive extension of the Epic 01 intake path that stays deterministic and local.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:135:- **AC-2.8**: A tool result arriving after its call's summary already landed with outcome `unknown` re-queues that summary at intake: the pair is the summary's source, and a source completing follows clear-and-regenerate like any source change. The check is deterministic and local (one indexed lookup by call id); the common case — call and result in one batch — never triggers it, because the summary runs after both landed.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:139:- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1): Intake a prompt, drain → smoothed form `ready`, content is the double's deterministic output for that input.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:142:- **TC-2.4** (AC-2.4): Three intake variants — result ok, result `isError`, call with no result → outcomes succeeded, failed, unknown; double's text identical across all three, proving text doesn't drive outcome.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:171:- **AC-3.9**: Chunk boundaries are deterministic: replaying the same record through the same policy values produces identical chunk membership.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:182:- **TC-3.8** (AC-3.8): Close a chunk, drain → detailed and brief summaries `ready`; double-marked content distinguishes them; detailed carries the run receipts fixture content, brief carries outcomes. Fail the brief item past budget with detailed succeeding → detailed `ready`, brief `failed`, independently re-queueable.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:203:- **AC-4.5**: Re-queueing is idempotent against the queue: asking for work already queued or in flight for the same form is a no-op, not a duplicate item.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:212:- **TC-4.4** (AC-4.4): Fail a smoothing past budget, re-queue through `messages`, drain with healthy double → `ready`, no failure residue.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:245:- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.4): Slow double processing old-content smoothing; edit mid-flight; let both complete → final form is post-edit content's smoothing.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:280:- **TC-6.5** (AC-6.5): Two-chunk thread, delete a turn from chunk 1, drain → chunk 1 summaries rebuilt from remaining turns (double input proves source set); chunk 2 forms untouched; boundaries identical.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:346:Every operation returns content or a structured failure carrying retryable-or-not. The deterministic test double implements all seven with marked, input-derived output and per-test failure injection.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:397:- All derivation behavior is testable without a network: the provider double is part of the shipped test surface.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:398:- Read-back is ordered and deterministic everywhere new records are added.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:410:7. Provider double injection ergonomics: per-test failure scripting without exposing test seams in production assembly.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:420:Provider seam interface and deterministic double; derivation state vocabulary as shared types; work-kind registry extension (`tool_call_summary`, `chunk_summary_detailed`, `chunk_summary_brief`); handler-map assembly at SDK construction; queue mechanical fields (claim, attempts) as schema migration on the Epic 01 table; fixtures for multi-state threads. Focused invariant tests on the double's determinism and the handler registry's unknown-kind behavior.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:426:**Boundary / risk notes:** Handlers in this story are minimal doubles landing marked artifacts; real derivation content arrives in Stories 2–3. Claim mechanics here are the cross-process safety Epic 1's seam promised.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:433:**Boundary / risk notes:** Adds `tool_call_summary` queueing at intake — touches Epic 01's intake path additively (batch result already reports queued work). The late-result re-queue check (AC-2.8) is the second intake touch: one indexed lookup, deterministic, same transaction.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:438:**Governing idea:** Composition consumes message-level forms and degrades gracefully where they are missing; chunk boundaries are deterministic and final.\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:4:// LHC_PROVIDER, looked up in the named-provider registry; no default and no\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:5:// silent no-op — an unresolvable provider is a caller error naming both the\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:20:    error: { errorClass: \"caller_error\", code: \"provider_not_configured\", reason },\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:27:  const name = providerFlag ?? process.env[\"LHC_PROVIDER\"];\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:30:      \"work drain needs a derivation provider: pass --provider <name> or set LHC_PROVIDER\",\npackages/lhc/src/cli/work.ts:36:      `no provider registered under \"${name}\" (--provider / LHC_PROVIDER); known: ${registeredProviderNames().join(\", \")}`,\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:13:  deterministicText,\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:89:  it(\"intake a prompt, drain → smoothed form ready with the double's deterministic output\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:90:    const double = createProviderDouble();\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:91:    const sdk = manualSdk(double);\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:118:        // The content is the double's pure function of the prompt text — the\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:120:        content: deterministicText(\"smoothPrompt\", { text }, text),\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:129:    expect(raw?.content).toBe(deterministicText(\"smoothPrompt\", { text }, text));\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:135:    const double = createProviderDouble();\npackages/lhc/test/derivation-messages.test.ts:136:    const captured =