kips it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:132:- One filter discipline, not per-site ad-hoc WHERE clauses — a shared filtered-read helper (or equivalent single point) so a new read path can't silently skip it.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:157:- [ ] Architecture-risk tests green: cascade-stops-at-chunk (TC-6.5), empty-chunk dropped-not-failed (TC-6.6), prompt protection (TC-6.3)\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:13:// (TC-6.6, architecture risk). Refusals — open turn, missing id, double\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:120:    chunks: unwrap(await turns.listChunks({ filePath })),\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:339:    const chunks = unwrap(await turns.listChunks({ filePath }));\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:341:    expect(chunks[0]?.memberTurnIds).toEqual([]);\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:414:    const liveChunks = unwrap(await turns.listChunks({ filePath }));\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:415:    expect(liveChunks.find((chunk) => chunk.chunkId === \"c1\")?.memberTurnIds).toEqual([\"t2\"]);\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:419:describe(\"TC-6.6 / AC-6.6 (architecture risk): an emptied chunk drops its summaries — absent, never failed\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:420:  it(\"deleting every turn in a chunk leaves an empty chunk with no summary rows, no queued rebuild, and clean reads\", async () => {\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:455:    // anywhere, no live work targeting the empty chunk.\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:461:    // Reads skip the empty chunk without error: it lists with zero members\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:463:    const chunks = unwrap(await turns.listChunks({ filePath }));\npackages/lhc/test/mutations-delete.test.ts:465:    expect(emptied?.memberTurnIds).toEqual([]);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
