s:77:  const sdk = createSdk({\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-mutations-delete.test.ts:80:    clock: () => new Date(\"2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z\"),\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-fix.test.ts:1:// Epic Fix Batch 1, process boundary: the strict-flag and blank-path guards\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-fix.test.ts:27:describe(\"Epic Fix Batch 1 (process boundary): CLI usage guards\", () => {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:33:- **FC-0.2**: Double determinism is proven: identical input to the same operation yields identical output across double instances; different operations are distinguishable in their marked output; failure injection drives fail-N-then-succeed, terminal failure, and latency per test configuration.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:45:Story 0 is the tech design's Chunk 0: the substrate every later story dispatches through. Three seams land inert-correct here. The **provider seam** (DD-7) is dependency injection at SDK construction — the deterministic double implements the same `DerivationProvider` interface production adapters will, so tests exercise the production seam, not a mock of internals. The **handler map** (DD-6) is the only join between the queue's opaque kinds and domain code; it assembles at `createSdk` from per-domain `workHandlers` tables. The **enqueue wrapper** (DD-5) makes \"queueing is what schedules processing\" structural: `enqueue` writes the work row *and* creates-or-resets the form's `pending` state row in the ambient transaction (enqueue is the only place form rows are created — completion is UPDATE-only), and registers the scheduler poke on `ctx.onCommit` — row, state, and poke all commit or all vanish together.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:70:| SDK assembly | `src/sdk.ts` (`createSdk(config)`: provider, mode, clock, retry/lease/chunk policy defaults) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:135:**Scheduler skeleton boundary:** manual mode is complete in this story (onCommit fires; scheduler poke is a no-op); background mode's single-flight/coalesce/catch-up behavior is Story 1's — the flag exists here so `createSdk` validates its config shape from day one.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:148:- Entrypoint: `createSdk(config)` — the only assembly path; provider, mode, and policy enter here.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:150:- Evidence: `test/fixtures.test.ts` constructs the SDK through `createSdk` with the double at the production seam; `pnpm run boundaries` proves the scheduler imports domain surfaces only through `domains/*/index.ts`.\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-projection.test.ts:1:// CLI process-boundary suite for message projection: TC-2.4's spawned-CLI\npackages/lhc/test/cli-process-projection.test.ts:50:describe(\"Story 3 (process boundary): projection through the spawned binary\", () => {\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:23:**Scope — out:** Delete (Story 6 — same cascade machinery, removal semantics on top). Open-turn mutations (refused; v1 boundary per the epic). Rebuild execution itself (the drain — Stories 1–3 machinery — runs the re-queued work; this story proves the queueing and the version check). Any generated thread-view refresh (none in this epic; DD-12).\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:50:The **source-version check** is the story's architectural heart and TC-5.4 is the epic's named architecture-risk test: a pre-edit item that completes after the edit writes through `forms.ts`'s version check, mismatches, and discards as `stale_discarded` (row deleted, outcome reported) — the post-edit rebuild stands regardless of completion order (AC-5.4). The rule in one line: a background result must not overwrite a derived form if the source changed since the job was queued. The check was built in Story 0, enforced from Story 2's first form write; this story is where it's finally *provoked*. Same machinery serves Story 6's deletes — the cascade module has two callers by design.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:70:| Cascade module | `src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts` (NEW: walk-and-clear, both mutation kinds parameterized) |\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:79:- [tech-design.md DD-8 (cascade module, one transaction, two callers)](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:87), line 87\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:114:Nothing past c: chunk summaries derive from their own members only — the cascade's reach is structural, not configured.\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:116:  createSdk,\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:246:describe(\"FC-0.1 (production seam): createSdk assembles with the double injected where production adapters go\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:247:  it(\"resolves config defaults centrally and carries the injected provider and mode\", () => {\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:249:    const sdk = createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \"manual\" });\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:250:    expect(sdk.config.provider).toBe(double);\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:251:    expect(sdk.config.mode).toBe(\"manual\");\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:252:    expect(sdk.config.retry).toEqual({ budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 5000, backoffCapMs: 60000 });\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:253:    expect(sdk.config.lease).toEqual({ durationMs: 120000 });\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:254:    expect(sdk.config.chunkPolicy).toEqual({\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:265:    const sdk = createSdk({ provider