{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Manual/background mode isolation is not preserved across SDK instances: a background SDK installs process-wide scheduler hooks and a later manual SDK does not clear them, so manual intake can drain automatically without an explicit drain call.\",\"Deletion flow does not fully compose with paired tool-call/tool-result derivation: deleted tool results are excluded from turn membership but can still be read by the pairing query, and stale tool-call summary metadata can survive into rebuilt turn renderings.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"SDK mode selection drifts from the architecture contract because scheduler execution is controlled through process-global mutable hooks instead of being isolated to the SDK instance that chose background mode.\",\"The deleted-read filter discipline misses the tool pairing read path, and the mutation cascade does not repair paired counterpart summaries even though Flow 2 makes the paired message a source dependency.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both required gates pass, and the implemented stories have broad test coverage, but the coverage misses cross-SDK mode isolation and delete/edit cases where a tool-call summary depends on a paired tool result.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No silent fake provider default was found: CLI drain requires --provider or LHC_PROVIDER, and the deterministic provider is explicit-only.\",\"Material production-path issue found: manual mode can execute through a background scheduler left by a prior SDK in the same process.\",\"Material production-path issue found: tool pairing can read deleted messages and produce real ready forms with outcomes derived from deleted records.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Manual SDK mode can auto-drain after background SDK construction\",\"evidence\":\"Verified by constructing a background SDK, then a manual SDK in the same process, ingesting one prompt through the manual SDK, and observing the queued work disappear without calling manual drain: queuedImmediately contained w-m1-prompt_smoothing-v1, then queuedAfterWait was empty and a ready smoothed_prompt form existed. Code path: src/sdk.ts installs setSchedulerPoke and setThreadTouch for background mode but manual mode does not clear them; src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts fires the global scheduler poke on enqueue; src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts fires the global thread touch; src/scheduler.ts responds by draining.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"epic.md AC-1.7\",\"tech-design.md DD-4\",\"tech-design.md Flow 1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deleted tool results can still determine tool-call outcomes\",\"evidence\":\"Verified by creating a turn with a tool_call and paired tool_result, draining, deleting the tool_result, draining again, and observing rebuilt turn rendering metadata still report the tool_call outcome as succeeded even though the live membership no longer includes the result. Requeuing the tool_call_summary after deletion still rebuilt outcome succeeded. Code path: src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts findPairedBlock joins message without m.deleted_at IS NULL; src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts stamps tool_call_summary outcome from that pair; src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts trusts ready summary metadata; src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts clears the deleted message and upward turn forms but does not clear the paired counterpart summary.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"epic.md AC-2.4\",\"epic.md Flow 6\",\"06-message-turn-delete.md AC-6.2\",\"06-message-turn-delete.md DoD\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The cascade contract needs a ruling or update for paired tool-call/tool-result dependencies: the current delete cascade description focuses on the deleted message's upward chain, while the derivation architecture makes the paired counterpart a real source dependency.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
